<title>MEXICO: Avantel says has signed 430 major clients.</title>
<headline>Avantel says has signed 430 major clients.</headline>
<dateline>MONTERREY, Mexico 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telephone company Avantel said it has signed 430 major corporate clients for when Mexico's long-distance market is opened to competition in January.</p>
<p>Avantel is a joint venture between Mexico's Grupo Financiero Banamex-Accival and U.S.-based MCI Communications Corp.. Telefonos de Mexico's long-standing monopoly on long-distance calls ends on January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>Avantel said in a company presentation that its corporate clients included Aeromexico, Televisa, Benavides, Grupo Industrial Saltillo and Grupo Protexa.</p>
<p>((--Daniel Perez, Monterrey bureau +528 345-7617))</p>
